IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sg-core`
IMPORT `sg-periods`

-- Companies Act 1967 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition (SSO informal consolidation, version in force 6/5/2026 to 20/10/2026):
-- Part 5, Division 1 -- Office and name (ss 142 to 144). Layer 1, part agent sgj.
-- Source file lines 11493-11591. The text is a rendering of the Act, not the official text.
--
-- HOW IT IS MODELLED. One company at a time. Each duty is a decision function over the facts a witness can state
-- (a MAYBE BOOLEAN: JUST TRUE is yes, JUST FALSE is the text saying no in its own words, NOTHING is "the text does not say") and,
-- where the text names the party and the act, a regulative rule. Each offence is two functions: whether the person is guilty, and
-- the penalty the text states. Periods are counted by sg-periods only (days, as the clock of the traces below).
-- "In default" and "officer" are taken as facts: s 4(1) "officer" is the keel's, and who is "in default" is not defined in the ranges read.

§ `Section 142: registered office of company`

DECLARE `s 142 act` IS ONE OF
    `s 142(1) have a registered office within Singapore from the date of incorporation`
    `s 142(1) keep the registered office open and accessible to the public for not less than 3 hours during ordinary business hours on each business day`

-- s 142(1): the two limbs of the duty, as one question: an office within Singapore from incorporation, open at least 3 hours on each business day.
-- src:11501 | 142.—(1) A company must as from the date of its incorporation
-- src:11502 | have a registered office within Singapore to which all
-- src:11503 | communications and notices may be addressed and which must be
-- src:11504 | open and accessible to the public for not less than 3 hours during
-- src:11505 | ordinary business hours on each business day.
@ref s 142(1) (src:11501-11505)
GIVEN `the company has had a registered office within Singapore since the date of its incorporation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the fewest hours on any business day for which the registered office has been open and accessible to the public during ordinary business hours` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 142(1) the company has a registered office as the subsection requires` MEANS
    IF    `the company has had a registered office within Singapore since the date of its incorporation`
      AND `the fewest hours on any business day for which the registered office has been open and accessible to the public during ordinary business hours` AT LEAST 3
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A company must as from the date of its incorporation have a registered office within Singapore ... which must be open and accessible to the public for not less than 3 hours during ordinary business hours on each business day" -- a duty: the provision's own question, so an unmet limb is the text's no (marginal reading (a)/(N2) in NOTES.md)

-- s 142(1), first limb as a regulative rule: the company has the office from the date of incorporation. The trace clock counts days from incorporation (time 0);
-- "as from the date of its incorporation" is read as a deadline of 0 days after it (fork F-j142-1).
-- src:11501 | 142.—(1) A company must as from the date of its incorporation
-- src:11502 | have a registered office within Singapore to which all
-- src:11503 | communications and notices may be addressed and which must be
-- src:11504 | open and accessible to the public for not less than 3 hours during
-- src:11505 | ordinary business hours on each business day.
@ref s 142(1) (src:11501-11505)
GIVEN `the name of the company` IS A STRING
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 142 act`
`s 142(1) the company must have a registered office from the date of its incorporation` MEANS
    PARTY Company `the name of the company`
    MUST `s 142(1) have a registered office within Singapore from the date of incorporation`
    WITHIN 0
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Company `the name of the company` BECAUSE "the company did not have a registered office within Singapore from the date of its incorporation"

-- s 142(1), second limb as a regulative rule: "on each business day" is a standing duty with no time limit and no consequence of its own, so no trace can breach it (NOTES.md, Rules with no breach path).
-- src:11501 | 142.—(1) A company must as from the date of its incorporation
-- src:11502 | have a registered office within Singapore to which all
-- src:11503 | communications and notices may be addressed and which must be
-- src:11504 | open and accessible to the public for not less than 3 hours during
-- src:11505 | ordinary business hours on each business day.
@ref s 142(1) (src:11501-11505)
GIVEN `the name of the company` IS A STRING
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 142 act`
`s 142(1) the company must keep the registered office open for 3 hours on each business day` MEANS
    PARTY Company `the name of the company`
    MUST `s 142(1) keep the registered office open and accessible to the public for not less than 3 hours during ordinary business hours on each business day`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    -- no LEST: s 142(1) states no time for this duty, so a breach needs a standard from elsewhere (Interpretation Act 1965 s 52: "with all convenient speed"); dropped clause: LEST BREACH BY Company `the name of the company` BECAUSE "the registered office was not open and accessible to the public for not less than 3 hours during ordinary business hours on a business day" (assumed, not ruled; see notes/lest-without-deadline.md)

-- s 142(2): the offence of default under (1).
-- src:11507 | (2) If default is made in complying with subsection (1), the
-- src:11508 | company and every officer of the company who is in default shall be
-- src:11509 | guilty of an offence and shall be liable on conviction to a fine not
-- src:11510 | exceeding $5,000 and also to a default penalty.
@ref s 142(2) (src:11507-11510)
GIVEN `default is made in complying with subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is an officer of the company who is in default` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 142(2) the person is guilty of the offence this subsection creates` MEANS
    IF    `default is made in complying with subsection (1)`
      AND (`the person is the company` OR `the person is an officer of the company who is in default`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If default is made in complying with subsection (1), the company and every officer of the company who is in default shall be guilty of an offence" -- an element is unmet, so the subsection makes the person guilty of nothing on these facts (split site (i), fork line F-j142-2)

@ref s 142(2) (src:11507-11510)
GIVEN `default is made in complying with subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is an officer of the company who is in default` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE Penalty
`s 142(2) the most the person may be sentenced to on conviction` MEANS
    IF `s 142(2) the person is guilty of the offence this subsection creates` `default is made in complying with subsection (1)` `the person is the company` `the person is an officer of the company who is in default` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    --                          fine, months, both, default penalty
    THEN JUST (Penalty OF 5000, 0, FALSE, TRUE)
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection states a penalty only for the person it makes guilty

§ `Section 143: office hours`

DECLARE `s 143 act` IS ONE OF
    `s 143(1) lodge notice of the change of the particulars of the registered office`

-- s 143(1), the main rule: what the notice states and when it is lodged for a proposed company. The exemption: no notice of the days and hours if the office is open at least 5 hours each business day.
-- src:11514 | 143.—(1) Notice in the prescribed form of the situation of the
-- src:11515 | registered office, the days and hours during which it is open and
-- src:11516 | accessible to the public, must, in the case of a proposed company, be
-- src:11521 | lodged with the Registrar together with its constitution, at the time of
-- src:11522 | lodgment for the incorporation of the proposed company and in the
-- src:11523 | case of any subsequent change of the particulars therein be so lodged
-- src:11524 | within 14 days after any such change, but no notice of the days and
-- src:11525 | hours during which the office is open and accessible to the public is
-- src:11526 | required if the office is open for at least 5 hours during ordinary
-- src:11527 | business hours on each business day.
@ref s 143(1) (src:11514-11527)
GIVEN `the fewest hours on any business day for which the registered office is open and accessible to the public during ordinary business hours` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 143(1) the notice must state the days and hours during which the office is open and accessible to the public` MEANS
    IF `the fewest hours on any business day for which the registered office is open and accessible to the public during ordinary business hours` AT LEAST 5
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "no notice of the days and hours during which the office is open and accessible to the public is required if the office is open for at least 5 hours during ordinary business hours on each business day"
    ELSE JUST TRUE    -- the notice must state the situation of the registered office and "the days and hours during which it is open and accessible to the public"

-- s 143(1), the proposed company: the notice is lodged with the constitution at the time of lodgment for incorporation.
@ref s 143(1) (src:11514-11527)
GIVEN `the notice was lodged together with the constitution at the time of lodgment for the incorporation of the proposed company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 143(1) the proposed company's notice was lodged as the subsection requires` MEANS
    IF `the notice was lodged together with the constitution at the time of lodgment for the incorporation of the proposed company`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must, in the case of a proposed company, be lodged with the Registrar together with its constitution, at the time of lodgment for the incorporation of the proposed company" -- a duty, the provision's own question

-- s 143(1): "in the case of any subsequent change of the particulars therein be so lodged within 14 days after any such change".
-- Not later than the 14th day after the change (sg-periods P1, P2: the day of the change is not counted; a notice lodged on the day itself is in time, fork F-j-periods).
@ref s 143(1) (src:11514-11527)
GIVEN `the day the particulars changed` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 143(1) the last day for lodging notice of a change of the particulars` MEANS
    `period: the last day of a period after` `the day the particulars changed` 14 Days

@ref s 143(1) (src:11514-11527)
GIVEN `the day the particulars changed` IS A DATE
      `the day the notice of the change was lodged` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 143(1) the notice of the change was lodged within 14 days after the change` MEANS
    IF `the day the notice of the change was lodged` AT MOST (`s 143(1) the last day for lodging notice of a change of the particulars` `the day the particulars changed`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "be so lodged within 14 days after any such change" -- a period the text fixes in its own words; outside it the answer is the text's no (periods ruling of 2026-11-05, item (a))

-- s 143(1), the deadline as a regulative rule. The trace clock counts days after the change (time 0 is the day of the change).
@ref s 143(1) (src:11514-11527)
GIVEN `the name of the company` IS A STRING
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 143 act`
`s 143(1) the company must lodge notice of a change of the particulars within 14 days` MEANS
    PARTY Company `the name of the company`
    MUST `s 143(1) lodge notice of the change of the particulars of the registered office`
    WITHIN 14
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Company `the name of the company` BECAUSE "the company did not lodge notice of the change of the particulars of its registered office within 14 days after the change"

-- s 143(1A): "particulars", in relation to the situation of the registered office, includes the address and the designation.
-- src:11531 | (1A) In subsection (1), the word “particulars”, in relation to the
-- src:11532 | situation of the registered office, includes the address and designation
-- src:11533 | of the situation or address of the registered office.
@ref s 143(1A) (src:11531-11533)
GIVEN `the item is the address of the registered office` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the item is the designation of the situation or address of the registered office` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 143(1A) "particulars" the item is within the particulars of the situation of the registered office` MEANS
    IF `the item is the address of the registered office` OR `the item is the designation of the situation or address of the registered office`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "includes the address and designation of the situation or address of the registered office" -- an open list, so another item is not covered

-- s 143(2): the offence of default under s 143.
-- src:11537 | (2) If default is made in complying with this section, the company
-- src:11538 | and every officer of the company who is in default shall be guilty of
-- src:11539 | an offence and shall be liable on conviction to a fine not exceeding
-- src:11540 | $5,000 and also to a default penalty.
@ref s 143(2) (src:11537-11540)
GIVEN `default is made in complying with section 143` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is an officer of the company who is in default` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 143(2) the person is guilty of the offence this subsection creates` MEANS
    IF    `default is made in complying with section 143`
      AND (`the person is the company` OR `the person is an officer of the company who is in default`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If default is made in complying with this section, the company and every officer of the company who is in default shall be guilty of an offence" -- an element is unmet (split site (i), fork line F-j143-1)

@ref s 143(2) (src:11537-11540)
GIVEN `default is made in complying with section 143` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is an officer of the company who is in default` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE Penalty
`s 143(2) the most the person may be sentenced to on conviction` MEANS
    IF `s 143(2) the person is guilty of the offence this subsection creates` `default is made in complying with section 143` `the person is the company` `the person is an officer of the company who is in default` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    --                          fine, months, both, default penalty
    THEN JUST (Penalty OF 5000, 0, FALSE, TRUE)
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection states a penalty only for the person it makes guilty

§ `Section 144: publication of name and registration number`

-- The things a company's name (s 144(1)) and registration number (s 144(1A)) must appear on, and the things s 144(2) names.
DECLARE `s 144 item` IS ONE OF
    `s 144 the company's seal`
    `s 144 a business letter`
    `s 144 a statement of account`
    `s 144 an invoice`
    `s 144 an official notice`
    `s 144 a publication`
    `s 144 a bill of exchange`
    `s 144 a promissory note`
    `s 144 an indorsement`
    `s 144 a cheque`
    `s 144 an order`
    `s 144 a receipt`
    `s 144 a letter of credit`
    `s 144 another negotiable instrument`
    `s 144 some other thing`

-- s 144(1): the name must appear in legible romanised letters on its seal, if any, and on the (b) documents.
-- The item list is not closed with "only", so a thing the paragraphs do not name is "not covered".
-- src:11544 | 144.—(1) The name of a company must appear in legible
-- src:11545 | romanised letters on —
-- src:11547 | (a) its seal, if any; and
-- src:11549 | (b) all business letters, statements of account, invoices, official
-- src:11550 | notices, publications, bills of exchange, promissory notes,
-- src:11551 | indorsements, cheques, orders, receipts and letters of credit
-- src:11552 | of or purporting to be issued or signed by or on behalf of
-- src:11553 | the company.
@ref s 144(1) (src:11544-11553)
GIVEN item IS A `s 144 item`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 144(1) the name of the company must appear on the item` MEANS
    CONSIDER item
    WHEN `s 144 the company's seal` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 144 a business letter` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 144 a statement of account` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 144 an invoice` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 144 an official notice` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 144 a publication` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 144 a bill of exchange` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 144 a promissory note` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 144 an indorsement` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 144 a cheque` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 144 an order` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 144 a receipt` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 144 a letter of credit` THEN JUST TRUE
    OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): paragraphs (a) and (b) list the things the name must appear on and do not say "only"

@ref s 144(1) (src:11544-11553)
GIVEN item IS A `s 144 item`
      `the company's name appears on the item in legible romanised letters` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 144(1) the company has complied with subsection (1) as to the item` MEANS
    IF `s 144(1) the name of the company must appear on the item` item EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN (IF `the company's name appears on the item in legible romanised letters`
          THEN JUST TRUE
          ELSE JUST FALSE)   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The name of a company must appear in legible romanised letters on" the listed items -- a duty, the provision's own question
    ELSE NOTHING             -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): the item is not one the paragraphs name

-- s 144(1A): the registration number must appear in a legible form on the shorter list (no seal, no bill of exchange or other instrument).
-- src:11557 | (1A) The registration number of a company must appear in a legible
-- src:11558 | form on all business letters, statements of account, invoices, official
-- src:11559 | notices and publications of or purporting to be issued or signed by or
-- src:11560 | on behalf of the company.
@ref s 144(1A) (src:11557-11560)
GIVEN item IS A `s 144 item`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 144(1A) the registration number of the company must appear on the item` MEANS
    CONSIDER item
    WHEN `s 144 a business letter` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 144 a statement of account` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 144 an invoice` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 144 an official notice` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 144 a publication` THEN JUST TRUE
    OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "all business letters, statements of account, invoices, official notices and publications" does not say "only"; a seal or an instrument is not named

@ref s 144(1A) (src:11557-11560)
GIVEN item IS A `s 144 item`
      `the company's registration number appears on the item in a legible form` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 144(1A) the company has complied with subsection (1A) as to the item` MEANS
    IF `s 144(1A) the registration number of the company must appear on the item` item EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN (IF `the company's registration number appears on the item in a legible form`
          THEN JUST TRUE
          ELSE JUST FALSE)   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The registration number of a company must appear in a legible form on" the listed items -- a duty, the provision's own question
    ELSE NOTHING             -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): the item is not one the subsection names

-- s 144(1B): "A company shall be guilty of an offence if default is made in complying with subsection (1) or (1A)."
-- src:11562 | (1B) A company shall be guilty of an offence if default is made in
-- src:11563 | complying with subsection (1) or (1A).
@ref s 144(1B) (src:11562-11563)
GIVEN `default is made in complying with subsection (1) or (1A)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is the company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 144(1B) the person is guilty of the offence this subsection creates` MEANS
    IF `default is made in complying with subsection (1) or (1A)` AND `the person is the company`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A company shall be guilty of an offence if default is made in complying with subsection (1) or (1A)" -- an element is unmet (split site (i), fork line F-j144-1)

-- s 144(1B) states no penalty: none appears in the subsection, and no other provision of the ranges read states one for it.
@ref s 144(1B) (src:11562-11563)
GIVEN `default is made in complying with subsection (1) or (1A)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is the company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE Penalty
`s 144(1B) the most the company may be sentenced to on conviction` MEANS
    NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): s 144(1B) creates the offence and states no fine; a general penalty, if any, is in a provision outside these ranges (fork F-j144-2)

-- s 144(2): an officer or any person on the company's behalf who uses a seal, or issues a document, without the name.
DECLARE `s 144(2) what the person did` IS ONE OF
    `s 144(2)(a) used or authorised the use of a seal purporting to be a seal of the company whereon its name does not appear in legible romanised letters`
    `s 144(2)(b) issued or authorised the issue of a business letter, statement of account, invoice, official notice or publication of the company wherein its name is not mentioned`
    `s 144(2)(c) signed, issued or authorised to be signed or issued on behalf of the company a bill of exchange, promissory note, cheque or other negotiable instrument or an indorsement, order, receipt or letter of credit wherein its name is not mentioned`
    `s 144(2) did something else`

-- src:11568 | (2) If an officer of a company or any person on its behalf —
-- src:11570 | (a) uses or authorises the use of any seal purporting to be a seal
-- src:11571 | of the company whereon its name does not so appear;
-- src:11573 | (b) issues or authorises the issue of any business letter,
-- src:11574 | statement of account, invoice or official notice or
-- src:11575 | publication of the company wherein its name is not so
-- src:11576 | mentioned; or
-- src:11578 | (c) signs, issues or authorises to be signed or issued on behalf
-- src:11579 | of the company any bill of exchange, promissory note,
-- src:11580 | cheque or other negotiable instrument or any indorsement,
-- src:11581 | order, receipt or letter of credit wherein its name is not so
-- src:11582 | mentioned,
-- src:11584 | he or she shall be guilty of an offence, and where he or she has signed,
-- src:11585 | issued or authorised to be signed or issued on behalf of the company
-- src:11586 | any bill of exchange, promissory note or other negotiable instrument
-- src:11587 | or any indorsement thereon or order wherein that name is not so
-- src:11588 | mentioned, he or she shall in addition be liable to the holder of the
-- src:11589 | instrument or order for the amount due thereon unless it is paid by the
-- src:11590 | company.
@ref s 144(2) (src:11568-11590)
GIVEN `the person is an officer of the company or a person acting on its behalf` IS A BOOLEAN
      act IS A `s 144(2) what the person did`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 144(2) the person is guilty of the offence this subsection creates` MEANS
    CONSIDER act
    WHEN `s 144(2)(a) used or authorised the use of a seal purporting to be a seal of the company whereon its name does not appear in legible romanised letters` THEN
        (IF `the person is an officer of the company or a person acting on its behalf` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE)   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If an officer of a company or any person on its behalf — (a) uses or authorises the use of any seal ... he or she shall be guilty of an offence" -- an element (the person's position) is unmet (split site (i), fork line F-j144-3)
    WHEN `s 144(2)(b) issued or authorised the issue of a business letter, statement of account, invoice, official notice or publication of the company wherein its name is not mentioned` THEN
        (IF `the person is an officer of the company or a person acting on its behalf` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE)   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): paragraph (b), same element (split site (i), fork line F-j144-3)
    WHEN `s 144(2)(c) signed, issued or authorised to be signed or issued on behalf of the company a bill of exchange, promissory note, cheque or other negotiable instrument or an indorsement, order, receipt or letter of credit wherein its name is not mentioned` THEN
        (IF `the person is an officer of the company or a person acting on its behalf` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE)   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): paragraph (c), same element (split site (i), fork line F-j144-3)
    OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): an act the three paragraphs do not name is not covered by this subsection

-- s 144(2): no penalty is stated for the offence in the subsection itself.
@ref s 144(2) (src:11568-11590)
GIVEN `the person is an officer of the company or a person acting on its behalf` IS A BOOLEAN
      act IS A `s 144(2) what the person did`
GIVETH A MAYBE Penalty
`s 144(2) the most the person may be sentenced to on conviction` MEANS
    NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): s 144(2) creates the offence and states no fine; a general penalty, if any, is in a provision outside these ranges (fork F-j144-2)

-- s 144(2), the additional civil liability: "where he or she has signed, issued or authorised to be signed or issued on behalf of the company any bill of exchange,
-- promissory note or other negotiable instrument or any indorsement thereon or order wherein that name is not so mentioned, he or she shall in addition be liable to the
-- holder of the instrument or order for the amount due thereon unless it is paid by the company."
DECLARE `s 144(2) the instrument` IS ONE OF
    `s 144(2) a bill of exchange`
    `s 144(2) a promissory note`
    `s 144(2) another negotiable instrument`
    `s 144(2) an indorsement on one of those`
    `s 144(2) an order`
    `s 144(2) a cheque`
    `s 144(2) a receipt`
    `s 144(2) a letter of credit`

@ref s 144(2) (src:11568-11590)
GIVEN instrument IS A `s 144(2) the instrument`
      `the person signed, issued or authorised to be signed or issued the instrument on behalf of the company, and the company's name is not mentioned in it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the amount due on the instrument has been paid by the company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 144(2) the person is liable to the holder of the instrument for the amount due on it` MEANS
    IF NOT `the person signed, issued or authorised to be signed or issued the instrument on behalf of the company, and the company's name is not mentioned in it`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the liability attaches to a person who signed, issued or authorised the instrument without the name
    ELSE CONSIDER instrument
         WHEN `s 144(2) a bill of exchange` THEN (IF `the amount due on the instrument has been paid by the company` THEN JUST FALSE ELSE JUST TRUE)   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless it is paid by the company"
         WHEN `s 144(2) a promissory note` THEN (IF `the amount due on the instrument has been paid by the company` THEN JUST FALSE ELSE JUST TRUE)   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless it is paid by the company"
